---
const dockerCmd = `docker run -d --name pooml --restart unless-stopped \\
  -e POOML_UI_SECRET=change-me-to-something-long-and-random \\
  -e POOML_ENCRYPTION_KEY=change-me-too-32-chars-minimum-ok \\
  -e POOML_DB_DIR=/data \\
  -p 8080:8080 -p 8081:8081 \\
  -v pooml-data:/data \\
  mykonordy/pooml:latest`;

const queries = [
  {
    label: 'errors across every service, last hour',
    sql: `SELECT * FROM logs
WHERE level >= 4 AND timestamp > unixepoch('now', '-1 hour') * 1000
ORDER BY timestamp DESC`,
  },
  {
    label: 'which service is the noisiest?',
    sql: `SELECT service, COUNT(*) AS lines
FROM logs GROUP BY service ORDER BY lines DESC`,
  },
  {
    label: 'p50-ish checkout latency, by hour',
    sql: `SELECT timestamp / 3600000 * 3600000 AS hour, AVG(value)
FROM metrics WHERE name = 'checkout_latency_seconds'
GROUP BY hour ORDER BY hour`,
  },
];

const envVars = [
  ['POOML_DB_DIR', 'required', 'Directory for the three SQLite files. Created if missing.'],
  ['POOML_UI_SECRET', 'required', 'UI login secret, min 32 chars.'],
  ['POOML_ENCRYPTION_KEY', 'required', 'Encrypts secrets stored in meta.db (S3 creds, tokens), min 32 chars.'],
  ['POOML_ENV', 'pro', 'local / pro. Cookie Secure flag, HSTS, log verbosity.'],
  ['POOML_API_ADDR', 'localhost:8080', 'Ingestion API bind address.'],
  ['POOML_UI_ADDR', 'localhost:8081', 'Web UI bind address.'],
  ['POOML_LOG_LEVEL', 'info', "pooml's own log level."],
  ['POOML_TRUST_PROXY_HEADERS', 'false', 'Read client IPs from X-Forwarded-For. Only behind a proxy that overwrites it.'],
  ['POOML_METRICS_ENABLED', 'false', "Expose pooml's own Prometheus metrics + self-scrape."],
  ['POOML_METRICS_AUTH_SECRET', '-', 'Required when metrics are enabled, min 32 chars.'],
  ['POOML_QUERY_API_ENABLED', 'false', 'Read-only SQL query API at /api/v1/query/*.'],
  ['POOML_QUERY_AUTH_SECRET', '-', 'Required when the query API is enabled, min 32 chars.'],
  ['POOML_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS', '30', 'Hard deadline for graceful shutdown.'],
];
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>pooml - the Poor Man's Logger</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Logs, metrics, dashboards, and alerts in one small SQLite-backed binary. Queried with plain SQL, built for self-hosters."
    />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/logo.png" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="pooml - the Poor Man's Logger" />
    <meta
      property="og:description"
      content="Logs + metrics in one binary. SQLite inside, SQL outside. No new query language to learn."
    />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://pooml.com/shots/dashboard.png" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://pooml.com" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <header class="hero">
        <div class="hero-text">
          <p class="eyebrow"><img class="logo" src="/logo.png" alt="" width="26" height="28" /> pooml <span class="dim">/&#712;pu&#720;ml/ &middot; the Poor Man's Logger</span></p>
          <h1><code>SELECT * FROM logs;</code></h1>
          <p class="tagline">
            That's the query language. pooml is a logs + metrics server in one
            small binary: SQLite inside, SQL outside, a web UI on top. Ship
            logs from FluentBit, push metrics over OTLP or scrape Prometheus
            endpoints, draw dashboards, get alerts on your phone.
          </p>
          <div class="cta-row">
            <a class="btn primary" href="https://github.com/n0rdy/pooml">GitHub &rarr;</a>
            <a class="btn" href="#quick-start">Quick start</a>
            <span class="license">AGPL-3.0 &middot; no telemetry</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </header>

      <figure class="shot">
        <img
          src="/shots/dashboard.png"
          alt="A pooml metrics dashboard: request rates by service, a queue-depth spike during an incident, and a big stat panel"
          width="1800"
          height="1075"
          loading="eager"
        />
        <figcaption>A real dashboard, five minutes after install. The spike is the demo incident.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <section class="why">
        <h2>No new query language. That's the feature.</h2>
        <p>
          Every observability tool ships its own query dialect: LogQL, PromQL,
          KQL, SPL, three flavors of Lucene. Each one you learn just well
          enough to forget by the next incident.
        </p>
        <p>
          pooml's query language shipped in 1974 and you already know it. Logs
          and metrics live in SQLite tables; you query them with <code>SELECT</code>, <code>WHERE</code>, <code>GROUP BY</code>, and friends. Full-text search rides on FTS5. A query builder exists for
          the lazy mornings, and it compiles to SQL you can read, edit, and
          keep.
        </p>
        <div class="queries">
          {queries.map((q) => (
            <div class="query-card">
              <p class="query-label">-- {q.label}</p>
              <pre><code>{q.sql}</code></pre>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mcp">
        <h2>Your AI assistant already speaks pooml</h2>
        <p>
          Because the query language is SQL, there's no custom DSL for an LLM
          to hallucinate around. <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pooml/mcp"><code>@pooml/mcp</code></a>
          connects Claude - or any MCP client - to your instance: strictly
          read-only, through the same SQL validation as the UI, credentials
          never leaving your machine. Ask <em>"what broke last night?"</em>
          and the model writes the query.
        </p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <pre><code>{`claude mcp add pooml \
  -e POOML_URL=https://your-pooml-host:8080 \
  -e POOML_QUERY_AUTH_SECRET=your-query-secret \
  -- npx -y @pooml/mcp`}</code></pre>
          <button class="copy" data-copy={`claude mcp add pooml -e POOML_URL=https://your-pooml-host:8080 -e POOML_QUERY_AUTH_SECRET=your-query-secret -- npx -y @pooml/mcp`}>copy</button>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="features">
        <h2>What's in the binary</h2>
        <div class="grid">
          <div class="feat">
            <h3>Logs</h3>
            <p>FluentBit-compatible ingestion, per-line format detection (JSON, CLF, plain), full-text search, live tail, infinite scroll.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feat">
            <h3>Metrics</h3>
            <p>OTLP/HTTP push and Prometheus scraping. Counters and gauges only, on purpose - histograms are downcast to their <code>_sum</code>/<code>_count</code> series. Query builder, charts with gap-aware series.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feat">
            <h3>Dashboards</h3>
            <p>Typed logs/metrics dashboards: stream, chart, and number panels. Panels remember the query that built them.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feat">
            <h3>Alerts</h3>
            <p>Alert rules are SQL queries too. Delivered via Pushover or Once Campfire, with cooldowns and an audit trail.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feat">
            <h3>Ops included</h3>
            <p>Hourly retention cleanup, scheduled S3 backups via SQLite's online backup API, Prometheus <code>/metrics</code> - pooml can monitor itself.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feat">
            <h3>Your data, in files</h3>
            <p>Three SQLite files you can copy, back up, or open with any SQLite tool. No telemetry, no phone-home, ever.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="peanuts">
        <h2>Runs on peanuts</h2>
        <p>
          Hence the mascot. One Go binary, three SQLite files, no JVM, no
          cluster, no sidecar agents. The whole thing idles in a few dozen
          megabytes of RAM and is perfectly happy on the cheapest VPS your
          cloud sells - the one that costs about as much as a bag of peanuts.
        </p>
        <figure class="shot small">
          <img
            src="/shots/logs.png"
            alt="The pooml logs view filtered to errors: a burst of stripe API timeouts during the demo incident"
            width="1800"
            height="1075"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption>The logs view during the same incident: <code>WHERE level &gt;= 3</code> and there's your story.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="honesty">
        <h2>pooml is not for everyone</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>It is <strong>not distributed</strong> and not highly available. One node, one binary, one disk.</li>
          <li>It is <strong>single-admin</strong>: one login secret, no user management, no RBAC.</li>
          <li>It is <strong>closed-contribution</strong>: open source, but no PRs - bugs and ideas go to GitHub Discussions.</li>
          <li>If you have a platform team and a compliance department, you want Grafana &amp; friends. Godspeed - they're great.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If you have three side projects on a VPS and grep-over-ssh has
          stopped being funny: welcome.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="quick-start" id="quick-start">
        <h2>Quick start</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <p>Run it:</p>
            <div class="code-block">
              <pre><code>{dockerCmd}</code></pre>
              <button class="copy" data-copy={dockerCmd}>copy</button>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p>Open <code>http://localhost:8081</code>, log in with your secret, mint an API key in Settings.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p>Point your log shipper at port 8080:</p>
            <div class="code-block">
              <pre><code>{`curl -X POST "http://localhost:8080/api/v1/ingest/my-service/my-host" \\
  -H "X-API-Key: $API_KEY" \\
  -d '{"level":"info","message":"hello pooml"}'`}</code></pre>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p class="aside">
          Binaries for Linux amd64/arm64 are on the <a href="https://github.com/n0rdy/pooml/releases">releases page</a>;
          building from source needs Go and the <code>sqlite_fts5</code> tag.
          The <a href="https://github.com/n0rdy/pooml#readme">README</a> covers
          FluentBit, OTLP, scrape targets, retention, and S3 backups.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="config">
        <h2>Configuration</h2>
        <p class="config-intro">
          Everything is environment variables. The required ones fail fast at
          startup with a clear message; the rest have defaults you can ignore.
        </p>
        <div class="env-table-wrap">
          <table class="env-table">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Variable</th><th>Default</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {envVars.map(([name, def, purpose]) => (
                <tr>
                  <td><code>{name}</code></td>
                  <td class="def">{def}</td>
                  <td>{purpose}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="used-by">
        <h2>Trusted in production</h2>
        <p class="used-by-intro">Real products keeping their logs in pooml.</p>
        <div class="used-by-row">
          <a class="used-by-card" href="https://retrek.me">
            <img src="/retrek.png" alt="" width="44" height="44" />
            <span class="used-by-text">
              <strong>reTrek</strong>
              <span>walking, made an adventure</span>
            </span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <footer>
        <a href="https://github.com/n0rdy/pooml">GitHub</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/n0rdy/pooml/blob/main/LICENSE">AGPL-3.0</a>
        <span class="dim">made by <a href="https://n0rdy.foo">n0rdy</a> &middot; this page has no analytics either</span>
      </footer>
    </main>

    <script>
      document.querySelectorAll('.copy').forEach((btn) => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(btn.dataset.copy);
          btn.textContent = 'copied';
          setTimeout(() => (btn.textContent = 'copy'), 1500);
        });
      });
    </script>

    <style>
      :root {
        --bg: #16191f;
        --surface: #1d232a;
        --edge: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.09);
        --text: #e8e4dd;
        --muted: #a49e93;
        --peanut: #c98a4b;
        --peanut-bright: #e4aa6d;
        --mono: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
      }
      * {
        margin: 0;
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }
      html {
        scroll-behavior: smooth;
      }
      body {
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--text);
        font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
        line-height: 1.6;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      }
      main {
        max-width: 1060px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 0 24px;
      }
      code {
        font-family: var(--mono);
      }
      h2 {
        font-size: 1.7rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
        text-wrap: balance;
      }
      section {
        margin: 5.5rem 0;
      }

      .hero {
        padding: 5.5rem 0 3rem;
      }
      .hero-text {
        flex: 1;
        min-width: 0;
      }
      .eyebrow {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 0.55rem;
        font-family: var(--mono);
        color: var(--peanut-bright);
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
      }
      .eyebrow .logo {
        width: 26px;
        height: auto;
      }
      .eyebrow .dim {
        color: var(--muted);
      }
      h1 {
        font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 4.6vw, 3.1rem);
        line-height: 1.15;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
        margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
        white-space: nowrap;
      }
      h1 code {
        color: var(--text);
      }
      .tagline {
        color: var(--muted);
        margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
      }
      .cta-row {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 0.9rem;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
      }
      .btn {
        display: inline-block;
        padding: 0.55rem 1.15rem;
        border-radius: 8px;
        border: 1px solid var(--edge);
        color: var(--text);
        text-decoration: none;
        font-weight: 500;
        transition: background-color 150ms ease-out, border-color 150ms ease-out;
      }
      .btn:hover {
        background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
      }
      .btn.primary {
        background: var(--peanut);
        border-color: var(--peanut);
        color: #16130e;
      }
      .btn.primary:hover {
        background: var(--peanut-bright);
        border-color: var(--peanut-bright);
      }
      .license {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.9rem;
      }

      .shot {
        margin: 2rem 0;
      }
      .shot img {
        width: 100%;
        height: auto;
        border-radius: 10px;
        outline: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
        outline-offset: -1px;
      }
      .shot figcaption {
        text-align: center;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        margin-top: 0.6rem;
      }

      .why p {
        color: var(--muted);
        margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
      }
      .why p code {
        color: var(--text);
      }
      .mcp p {
        color: var(--muted);
        margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
      }
      .mcp p code,
      .mcp p em {
        color: var(--text);
      }
      .mcp a {
        color: var(--peanut-bright);
      }
      .queries {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(290px, 1fr));
        gap: 1rem;
        margin-top: 1.6rem;
      }
      .query-card {
        background: var(--surface);
        border-radius: 10px;
        padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
        outline: 1px solid var(--edge);
        outline-offset: -1px;
        overflow-x: auto;
      }
      .query-label {
        font-family: var(--mono);
        color: var(--peanut-bright);
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
        white-space: nowrap;
      }
      .query-card pre {
        font-family: var(--mono);
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        line-height: 1.5;
        color: var(--text);
      }

      .grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
        gap: 1rem;
        margin-top: 1.4rem;
      }
      .feat {
        background: var(--surface);
        border-radius: 10px;
        padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem;
        outline: 1px solid var(--edge);
        outline-offset: -1px;
      }
      .feat h3 {
        font-size: 1.02rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
      }
      .feat p {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.93rem;
      }
      .feat code {
        font-size: 0.88em;
      }

      .peanuts p {
        color: var(--muted);
      }
      .shot.small {
        margin-top: 1.8rem;
      }

      .honesty ul {
        color: var(--muted);
        padding-left: 1.2rem;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
      }
      .honesty li {
        margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
      }
      .honesty strong {
        color: var(--text);
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      .quick-start ol {
        padding-left: 1.3rem;
        max-width: 800px;
      }
      .quick-start li {
        margin-bottom: 1.3rem;
      }
      .quick-start li > p {
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
      }
      .code-block {
        position: relative;
        background: var(--surface);
        border-radius: 10px;
        outline: 1px solid var(--edge);
        outline-offset: -1px;
        padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
        overflow-x: auto;
      }
      .code-block pre {
        font-family: var(--mono);
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        line-height: 1.55;
      }
      .copy {
        position: absolute;
        top: 0.6rem;
        right: 0.6rem;
        font-family: var(--mono);
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.07);
        color: var(--text);
        border: 1px solid var(--edge);
        border-radius: 6px;
        padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
        cursor: pointer;
      }
      .copy:hover {
        background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
      }
      .aside {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.92rem;
        margin-top: 1.4rem;
      }
      .aside a,
      .honesty a {
        color: var(--peanut-bright);
      }

      .config-intro {
        color: var(--muted);
        margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
      }
      .env-table-wrap {
        background: var(--surface);
        border-radius: 10px;
        outline: 1px solid var(--edge);
        outline-offset: -1px;
        overflow-x: auto;
      }
      .env-table {
        width: 100%;
        border-collapse: collapse;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
      }
      .env-table th,
      .env-table td {
        text-align: left;
        padding: 0.55rem 1rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--edge);
        vertical-align: top;
      }
      .env-table tbody tr:last-child td {
        border-bottom: none;
      }
      .env-table th {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-weight: 500;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
      }
      .env-table code {
        font-size: 0.85em;
        white-space: nowrap;
      }
      .env-table .def {
        font-family: var(--mono);
        color: var(--muted);
        white-space: nowrap;
        font-size: 0.85em;
      }
      .env-table td:last-child {
        color: var(--muted);
      }

      .used-by-intro {
        color: var(--muted);
        margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
      }
      .used-by-row {
        display: flex;
        gap: 1rem;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
      }
      .used-by-card {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 0.85rem;
        background: var(--surface);
        border-radius: 10px;
        outline: 1px solid var(--edge);
        outline-offset: -1px;
        padding: 0.9rem 1.2rem;
        text-decoration: none;
        color: var(--text);
        transition: background-color 150ms ease-out;
      }
      .used-by-card:hover {
        background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
      }
      .used-by-card img {
        width: 44px;
        height: 44px;
        border-radius: 10px;
      }
      .used-by-text {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        line-height: 1.35;
      }
      .used-by-text strong {
        font-weight: 600;
      }
      .used-by-text span {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.88rem;
      }

      footer {
        display: flex;
        gap: 1.4rem;
        align-items: center;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        padding: 2.5rem 0 3rem;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--edge);
        margin-top: 5rem;
        font-size: 0.92rem;
      }
      footer a {
        color: var(--text);
      }
      footer .dim {
        color: var(--muted);
        margin-left: auto;
      }
      footer .dim a {
        color: var(--muted);
      }

      @media (max-width: 760px) {
        .hero {
          padding-top: 3rem;
        }
        h1 {
          white-space: normal;
        }
        footer .dim {
          margin-left: 0;
        }
      }
      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        html {
          scroll-behavior: auto;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
